  "scientific_result": "Task 15 is an infrastructure task; it makes no new scientific claim. It unifies Tasks 6-14's nine independently-evolved result-JSON formats into one shared schema (evaluation.schema.validate_result: 9 fields required in every one of Tasks 6-14's existing result files -- task, implementation_status, seed, config, metrics, scientific_result, software_versions, tests, artifacts -- with every task-specific field Tasks 6-14 actually used kept as a documented optional extension, never dropped), plus one CLI dispatcher (evaluation.run_task, 'python -m evaluation.run_task --task 6..14') that imports and calls each task's existing experiment main() unchanged -- no experiment logic was rewritten to fit this framework. Re-validating all nine existing result files against the new schema found zero validation errors and zero required migrations: every file already used the field names the unified schema requires, so none was modified on disk (sha256 before == sha256 after for all nine, see migration_report and tests/test_evaluation_schema.py's git-diff check) and no previously recorded metric value from any of Tasks 6-14 changed. None of Tasks 6-14's own scientific findings (positive or negative) were re-derived, re-run, or reinterpreted by this task.",
